  "name": null,
  "problem": "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $-5$ | $-\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=4.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}",
